The Great Emu War · 3D YouTube Short (1080×1920), style v4 "Toon 3D"

Picture: modelled, lit and animated in code with three.js (MIT). Post (depth of field, bloom, grade): core/three/post.js from
the Lemo-Opuscar library (github.com/lemomo-ai/lemo-opuscar, MIT). Toon cast with hand-drawn canvas faces (toon.js), toon emus
with painted eyes and an instanced flock (emu.js), the outback, the army camp, the 1930s truck, the Lewis guns and the army
office (sets_emu.js). The people are stylised stand-ins with no real likeness; the uniforms, truck and guns are generic
period designs.

Style: techniques studied from a reference Short supplied by the creator (see toon-3d/style/REFERENCE.md); characters, designs,
story and assets here are original.

Voice-over: ElevenLabs v4 (voice preset "Harrison") through the creator's Higgsfield account; pauses tightened and sped up 28 %
(pitch unchanged) in timing.py. Check Higgsfield's / ElevenLabs' terms for your use.

Fonts: Montserrat (SIL OFL 1.1, fonts/OFL-Montserrat.txt); Fredoka (SIL OFL 1.1, fonts/OFL-Fredoka.txt).
Music and sound effects: synthesised in code (music.py; synth_lib.py from the Lemo-Opuscar library, MIT). No samples.
